00:05:30.578 --> 00:05:34.458
Jerais' first question,
Jerais is a long-time viewer.

00:05:34.458 --> 00:05:37.828
Is there a set process
that reliably, consistently

00:05:37.828 --> 00:05:41.995
works for everyone on turning
a business idea into reality?

00:05:43.437 --> 00:05:47.285
- Yeah, I think there's some golden rules.

00:05:47.285 --> 00:05:49.125
I wouldn't say there's
a cookie cutter process

00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:50.884
but there's some golden rules.

00:05:50.884 --> 00:05:53.385
Kind of rule number one is
always live in the shoes

00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:57.552
of your customer whether
it's a product or service.

00:05:59.894 --> 00:06:02.150
And that rule never goes
away as you grow and scale

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.216
your business, actually.

00:06:03.216 --> 00:06:05.514
You live in the shoes of your customer,

00:06:05.514 --> 00:06:08.252
you know, really be where your audience is

00:06:08.252 --> 00:06:09.643
and that's the start of everything.

00:06:09.643 --> 00:06:12.180
Now, I, we've talked
about, and I love this,

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.971
if you've got something you
really get frustrated by

00:06:16.971 --> 00:06:19.752
with a service that you're
receiving or a company

00:06:19.752 --> 00:06:23.017
you deal with, think about how
do you disintermediate that

00:06:23.017 --> 00:06:24.980
or do that a lot better than they can do

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.009
and then make that happen.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:28.500
And a lot of businesses have
been created just through

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.985
the genius of people who
have become very frustrated.

00:06:31.985 --> 00:06:34.640
So, I think the key thing
is golden rule number one

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:37.256
is just be where your customers
are and then have that

00:06:37.256 --> 00:06:41.269
sort of biased reaction
to think of your idea

00:06:41.269 --> 00:06:43.339
and then test drive it with,

00:06:43.339 --> 00:06:44.929
hopefully, early adopter customers

00:06:44.929 --> 00:06:46.083
to make sure it's real.

00:06:46.083 --> 00:06:47.642
If it's real, let's get it up.

00:06:47.642 --> 00:06:50.797
- Yeah, I would add, I think
you've got to make sure

00:06:50.797 --> 00:06:52.151
you take an action.

00:06:52.151 --> 00:06:54.233
I think a lot of entrepreneurs
have ideas but we're talking

00:06:54.233 --> 00:06:56.815
in this episode how to
turn it into reality.

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:59.644
It's taking consistent action,
it's waking up everyday

00:06:59.644 --> 00:07:01.603
and doing something to
move your business forward

00:07:01.603 --> 00:07:03.937
even if you feel like it's too big an idea

00:07:03.937 --> 00:07:05.204
or it's too scary.

00:07:05.204 --> 00:07:06.808
I think a lot of times
people are so worried about

00:07:06.808 --> 00:07:09.463
taking the perfect first step
that they don't do anything,

00:07:09.463 --> 00:07:10.564
where there is no perfect first step,

00:07:10.564 --> 00:07:13.266
it's just go out and do.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:16.564
And like Steven started a vlog
on our last episode, right?

00:07:16.564 --> 00:07:17.496
- Yeah, yeah.

00:07:17.496 --> 00:07:20.071
- Like 20 days ago he started
a vlog and you've done

00:07:20.071 --> 00:07:21.255
a second episode.

00:07:21.255 --> 00:07:22.088
- Yep.

00:07:22.088 --> 00:07:22.921
- And you're doing a third one here?

00:07:22.921 --> 00:07:23.754
- Yep.

00:07:23.754 --> 00:07:25.017
- And, it's just, we're
going to get started

00:07:25.017 --> 00:07:26.779
and we're going to learn each time.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:28.495
And you're like, hey, give us
feedback and then we're going to

00:07:28.495 --> 00:07:29.925
do it again and do it
again and do it again

00:07:29.925 --> 00:07:31.845
and every time you do it, it gets better.

00:07:31.845 --> 00:07:34.338
You know, there's no
perfect way to start a vlog,

00:07:34.338 --> 00:07:36.840
you just get a camera out
and you start vlogging

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:37.986
and you make improvements every time.

00:07:37.986 --> 00:07:40.151
And so I think a lot of times
entrepreneurs are in their

00:07:40.151 --> 00:07:42.932
own way, in their own head
too much worrying about

00:07:42.932 --> 00:07:45.379
how do I get started,
what first step do I take?

00:07:45.379 --> 00:07:47.431
Just do something and
then tomorrow do it again,

00:07:47.431 --> 00:07:49.756
and do it again, and every time
you get a little bit better.

00:07:49.756 --> 00:07:53.240
That consistency is going
to be really important.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.024
- Yeah, and I think, I
know a lot of entrepreneurs

00:07:56.024 --> 00:07:59.387
and I'll say, and sometimes
I'd say this about me,

00:07:59.387 --> 00:08:01.757
one of the things I'll
be critical of myself,

00:08:01.757 --> 00:08:03.961
is sometimes, you know,
I do seek perfection.

00:08:03.961 --> 00:08:06.331
Reality is, you know, we'll
probably never find perfection

00:08:06.331 --> 00:08:07.581
on this planet.

00:08:08.923 --> 00:08:12.317
And if you're looking to
have the perfect product

00:08:12.317 --> 00:08:16.085
or the perfect sort of
market research or trialing

00:08:16.085 --> 00:08:18.785
or whatever, you're just
never going to do that

00:08:18.785 --> 00:08:20.667
and you're going to spin
yourself in circles.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:22.846
You're much better off doing
exactly what Evan said,

00:08:22.846 --> 00:08:26.854
is just that action, that
action orientation to start.

00:08:26.854 --> 00:08:30.822
And, you know, on that video,
vlog, that we're doing,

00:08:30.822 --> 00:08:33.354
